abstract: >-
  Routines and raw spectra for the quasinormal modes of a massive scalar field around a Schwarzschild black hole. The
  two-sheeted relation between frequency and wave number at infinity is uniformised by a Joukowski map, and a
  Chebyshev collocation turns the radial problem into a polynomial eigenvalue problem of degree seven, assembled in
  Maple and solved in MATLAB with the Advanpix toolbox at three resolutions and precisions; two Python scripts check
  the results by continued fractions and check the effective potential. The spectra of 47 pairs of mass and multipole
  are included with their convergence reports.
